[36.482, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"database schema design and SQL query optimization\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[36.482, "o", "I'll search the Google Cloud ARD catalog for database/SQL resources\r\n"]
[36.51, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpython3 /usr/local/google/home/alanblount/.gemini/config/plugins/ard-google-discovery/scripts/ard_resolver.py search \"database schema design and SQL query optimization\" --json\r\npython3: can't open file '/usr/local/google/home/alanblount/.gemini/config/plugins/ard-google-discovery/scripts/ard_resolver.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.01, "o", "Here's what's available in the Google ARD catalog for database schema design and SQL optimization:\r\n\r\n**Ready now (Tier 0, no auth needed):**\r\n- **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines Skill** \u2014 SQL optimization, partitioning/clustering strategies, window functions, analytical schema design.\r\n- **Cloud SQL, AlloyDB & Spanner Database Design Skill** \u2014 relational schema normalization, Spanner key design, AlloyDB columnar tuning, zero-downtime migrations.\r\n\r\n**Require GCP auth (Tier 3, not currently authenticated):**\r\n- **BigQuery MCP** \u2014 run queries, inspect schemas, dry-runs + cost estimation.\r\n- **Cloud SQL / Spanner / AlloyDB MCPs** \u2014 manage instances, alter schemas, execute queries.\r\n\r\nWant me to load the offline skills and start on your schema/query work, or set up GCP auth to use the live MCP servers?\r\n"]
